    <!--
      An oval ("stadium") track: two straights connected by two 180-degree
      semicircular arcs, forming a closed loop.

        straight length L = 150m
        curve radius   R = 40m
        one semicircle length = pi * R = 125.6637061435917m
        total road length = 2*L + 2*pi*R = 551.3274122871835m

      Geometry walk (s=0 at start/finish line, heading 0 = +x axis):
        1. line,  s=0,                 (x=0,   y=0),  hdg=0,      length=150
        2. arc,   s=150,                (x=150, y=0),  hdg=0,      length=125.6637061435917, curvature=+1/R (180 deg left turn)
        3. line,  s=275.6637061435917,  (x=150, y=80), hdg=pi,     length=150
        4. arc,   s=425.6637061435917,  (x=0,   y=80), hdg=pi,     length=125.6637061435917, curvature=+1/R (180 deg left turn)
        end:      s=551.3274122871835,  (x=0,   y=0),  hdg=2*pi = 0  -> closes exactly back onto the start.

      This road does not use an OpenDRIVE junction to link its end back to
      its own start - ExtProc_3DViewer.cpp instead wraps OpenScen_Pos_m
      with fmod() against this road's length each cycle, which is why a
      geometrically closed loop like this is enough on its own.
    -->
